      Polymeric Stone Dust vs. Sand for Irregular Flagstone Patios
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      When building a patio with irregular, natural cleft flagstone, joints rarely adhere to the neat, uniform 1/8-inch gaps of manufactured concrete pavers. Gaps meander unpredictably from 1/2 inch to 3 or 4 inches wide. Filling these massive voids with standard polymeric paver sand results in catastrophic washout, weed infestation, and cracked joints. Here is the engineering science between <strong>polymeric stone dust (Gator Dust) and standard paver sand</strong>.
    </p>

