  <!-- Trade Field Note -->
  <FieldNote
    expertName="David Miller, PE"
    role="Senior Structural & Geotechnical Engineer"
    experience="25+ Years Field Experience"
    avatarBg="bg-blue-100 text-blue-800"
    initials="DM"
    title="Why Flagstone Must Be 100% Bone Dry Before You Open the First Bag"
    note="The most common mistake DIY patio builders make is installing polymeric dust after a morning dew or a rain shower yesterday because 'the stones look mostly dry.' Natural stone is porous like a sponge; it holds internal capillary moisture long after the top looks dry. If you dump polymeric stone dust onto damp stone, the water-activated polymers immediately start cross-linking ON THE SURFACE before the dust ever falls into the joint! You end up with a sticky, gummy mess that clings to stone faces and cannot be swept into the seams. Check the forecast for 48 hours of uninterrupted sunshine, make sure the stones have dried in full sun for at least 8 hours, and confirm that joint gaps are bone dry to their full 2-inch depth."
  />

